MajorDuties:
As a INTELLIGENCE SPECIALIST (CHIEF OF STAFF) you will be responsible for the following duties: - Reviewing, assigning and tracking tasks assigned from DCSA HQ, other agency directorates and DoD organizations using the Correspondence and Task Management System (CATMS);
- Coordinating with DCSA HQ and other internal organizations to ensure effective communications are maintained and CI interests are represented; - Developing, coordinating, and tracking internal and external staff actions to ensure timely, efficient actions are processed within established guidance and processes; - Working with senior staff members, action officers, managers, team leaders, and operating officials to ensure proper response to CI actions and to resolve or mitigate both short and long term issues;
- Leading initiatives within CI to ensure effective cross-agency integration for risk-based analysis and mitigation decisions.

MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GG/GS-12 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector performing duties such as: 1) Performing all-source research and analysis to produce integrated all-source intelligence products;
2) Writing intelligence assessments that comply with the Intelligence Community's analytic tradecraft standards;
3) Demonstrated experience facilitating/mentoring analysts in the production of all-source intelligence assessments using Structured Analytic Techniques, Analytic Design, and/or other IC analytic tools, methods and frameworks;
4) Experience leading internal or external working groups to address analytic issues;
5) Conducting independent intelligence research and analysis focused on developing countries threat force capabilities, threat tendencies, and vulnerabilities. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management website: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series
